obs MECHANISM. settlement/replay.rye folds each fixed-width event onto the preceding 32-byte SHA3-256 digest. Spawn, adoption and transfer update bounded visible state and then enter the fold in declared order. The cadence roster names tools/s/settlement_replay_witness.rish, which builds the binary it runs.
obs BOTH SIDES ON METAL. Spawn-adopt-transfer returned ordered digest 838eaa9fadea29d31a52c33d2985dda4e767c0e2aaae7c31afb9b1dc8d33a6f6 on both complete runs. Spawn-transfer-adopt kept sponsor 15 and keeper 42 equal yet returned f81337bb0059a522202b8222220ca36b27e1922343dead1e82d2cd57c77567a3. Transfer before spawn refused NotSpawned.
obs THE GUARD REFUSED A BYPASS. A compiling planted fold that hashed the constant word blind instead of its events exited 1 under the same witness. Restoring the event bytes returned GREEN. An earlier plant discarded the fold buffer and failed at compile time; that was too shallow to prove the semantic seam, so it was replaced rather than counted as the refusal.
